        "# Numerical Example\n",
        "\n",
        "A reproducible experiment for the manuscript studies function-on-scalar regression with a martingale score.\n",
        "\n",
        "Seeds and sample sizes are explicit. The design starts at $X_1=0$. The continuous $L^2$ error is computed exactly from the orthonormal noise coefficients. No replication is silently dropped. Figures and machine-readable results are exported to `tvc_outputs/`.\n",
        "\n",
        "The experiment illustrates the theoretical results over the sample sizes considered.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Setting\n",
        "\n",
        "The single-path experiment uses $n=5000$ and seed 54321. The Monte Carlo experiment uses 100 paths of length 3000 and master seed 20260922. Both retain $K=64$ noise coordinates.\n",
        "\n",
        "For a path with seed $s$, the design and Gaussian coordinate $k$ use PCG64 streams initialized by SeedSequence with inputs $[s,101]$ and $[s,202,k]$, respectively. The coefficient functions are displayed on 1001 grid points.\n"
      ],
