        "\n",
        "# Function-on-scalar regression with martingale score\n",
        "\n",
        "We simulate\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Y_n^{(K)}(t)=X_n^\\top\\beta_0(t)+\\varepsilon_n^{(K)}(t),\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\beta_0\\in\\mathbb H^3,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "with predictable serially dependent covariates $X_n$ and functional errors\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\varepsilon_n^{(K)}(t)=\\sigma_n\\sum_{k=1}^K k^{-1}Z_{nk}\\sqrt{2}\\sin(k\\pi t),\n",
        "\\qquad \\sigma_n=0.65+0.20\\tanh(X_{n1}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "The score uses these truncated errors. They satisfy\n",
        "$$\n",
        "E(\\varepsilon_n^{(K)}\\mid\\mathcal{F}_{n-1})=0.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Therefore\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D_n^{(K)}=X_n\\varepsilon_n^{(K)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "is an $\\mathbb H^3$-valued martingale-difference sequence.\n",
        "\n",
        "The numerical diagnostics check:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Q_n=\\frac1n\\sum_{i=1}^nX_iX_i^\\top,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\lambda_{\\min}(Q_n),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "the conditional-moment series\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\sum_n n^{-2\\rho}\n",
        "E(\\|D_n^{(K)}\\|_{\\mathbb H^3}^2\\mid\\mathcal{F}_{n-1}),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "and the almost-sure rate suggested by the theorem,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "n^{1-\\rho}\n",
        "\\|\\widehat\\beta_n^{(K)}-\\beta_0\\|_{\\mathbb H^3}\\to0,\n",
        "\\qquad \\rho>1/2.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "For the present design, the limiting design matrix can be identified explicitly. Since each coordinate satisfies\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "X_{n,j}=aX_{n-1,j}+(1-a)U_{n-1,j},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "with $E(U_{n,j})=0$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(U_{n,j})=1/3$, the stationary variance is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "q\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{(1-a)^2/3}{1-a^2}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1-a}{3(1+a)}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The coordinates are independent and identically distributed, so\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Q=E(X_n^*(X_n^*)^\\top)=qI_3,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For $a=0.65$,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\lambda_{\\min}(Q)=q\\approx 0.0707>0.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus the theoretical design limit is positive definite. The plot of $\\lambda_{\\min}(Q_n)$ should approach this positive limit; it is not merely a numerical nonsingularity check.\n",
        "\n",
        "Here $X_n^*$ denotes the stationary version. The simulated design starts at $X_1=0$ and is not stationary at finite n; its empirical second moment converges to the same Q because the initial transient decays geometrically.\n"
      ]
